<< part(3, "Objectives and measurable success criteria") >>

*Objectives.* (O1) Name the group containing the failed part accurately, on as-new and aged units; (O2) with less effort to a confirmed answer than scripted troubleshooting; (O3) with its uncertainty shown: calibrated probabilities, visible ambiguity groups and an explicit "no single fault fits"; (O4) safely: no unsafe step or invented reading; (O5) practically: fast, cheap, reading plain complaints and meter photos. T1-T7 test O1, T8-T11 O2, T12-T14 and T22-T23 O3, T15-T17 O4, T18-T21 O5.

*Effort.* A DC reading costs << num(m('library.design.cost_dc'), 0) >> unit, an oscilloscope measurement << num(m('library.design.cost_scope'), 0) >>, a point that can exceed 50 V << num(m('library.design.cost_hv_extra'), 0) >> more (leads clipped on with the power off, then powered, read and powered down) and unsoldering a part << num(m('library.design.cost_lift'), 0) >>, within a budget of << num(m('library.design.budget'), 0) >>. A technician replaces a part only after confirming it, so every method is charged one unsoldering test of its named suspect unless it has already unsoldered and confirmed one. The weights are estimates: every comparison is repeated with the scope, unsoldering and high-voltage weights halved and doubled, and the boards will time the low-voltage steps.

